        "Documents produced in mainland China, overseas areas, or Hong Kong and Macau must be authenticated by the Straits Exchange Foundation (SEF), overseas missions, or the Taipei Economic and Cultural Office (Hong Kong, Macau). Documents submitted in a foreign language must be authenticated by overseas missions and accompanied by a verified Chinese translation; vaccination certificates in a foreign language must be transcribed and registered at the competent health center. Applicants for an Employment Gold Card under Article 9 applied mutatis mutandis pursuant to Article 24 of the Act are exempt.",
